'''Xilawa Dater''' was a [[human]] who was a [[youngling]] in the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. In [[132 BBY]], she was part of a class in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]]. Sol had the students [[Meditation|meditate]] and connect with [[the Force]], telling them to state what they saw. Dater saw the Force as life, and Sol approved of her interpretation before dismissing the class for [[Foodstuff|lunch]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|Connect to the Force. Have faith. Think of diving into a great ocean. Give yourselves over to its weight, its stillness, its uncertainty. And tell me what comes into your mind.|Sol instructs Dater and her class|audio=Sol-ConnectToTheForce-LostFound.flac|<ref name="LostFound" />}}
[[File:XilawaDater-LostFound.png|thumb|right|300px|alt=Xilawa Dater, wearing tan Jedi robes, sits with her eyes closed among several other students on the floor of a training veranda in the Coruscant Jedi Temple. Behind them, the green-skinned Vernestra Rwoh stands in gold and yellow temple robes.|Xilawa Dater was a Jedi youngling on Coruscant during the High Republic Era.]]
Xilawa Dater was a [[human]] member of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. While a [[youngling]], she performed exercises in the [[Jedi temple arboretum|Temple arboreta]] that demonstrated her strong sense of life.<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> she<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> attended a lesson with other [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] on a training veranda in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. The lesson was led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]], who instructed Dater and the others to [[Meditation|meditate]] and close their [[eye]]s, stating that their sight could not be trusted, as it could be deceived.<ref name="LostFound" />

Sol then instructed the younglings to connect to [[the Force]] and tell him what entered their minds. Dater stated that she saw life, and Sol responded approvingly. After the student<ref name="LostFound" /> [[Jev Eremia]] said he<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> saw [[fire]], Sol explained that the Force was powerful like a fire or an [[ocean]] and so must be respected. By this point, the Jedi Master [[Vernestra Rwoh]] had entered the veranda to speak with Sol, and so he called the lesson to an end, dismissing Dater and the rest of the class for [[Foodstuff|lunch]]. She opened her eyes and stood. filing out with the others and bowing to Rwoh before being shepherded away by<ref name="LostFound" /> [[Jedi Knight]] [[Flurri Wiss]]<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> and another [[Jedi]].<ref name="LostFound" />

==Personality and traits==
Xilawa Dater had a strong sense of life, demonstrating it in the arboreta<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> and perceived the Force as it when meditating.<ref name="LostFound" /> She had tan skin, [[Color|black]] [[hair]], and brown eyes.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Equipment==
During her lesson with Sol, Dater wore tan [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]] with a brown [[belt]] and brown shoes.<ref name="LostFound" /> The belt's gray buckle bore a seal of the late High Republic.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Xilawa Dater was portrayed by [[Danielle Xin Yao Waterman]] in "[[Lost / Found]],"<ref name="LostFound" /> the first episode of the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-teaser-poster|text=''The Acolyte'' Teaser Poster, Premiere Date Revealed}}</ref>  Prior to the release of the episode, she was revealed in a trailer exclusively shown at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]<ref name="Celebration">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="CelebrationDate">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> The scenes in the Jedi Temple were shot at [[Shinfield Studios]],<ref name="Fantha Part I">{{WebCite|url=https://www.fanthatracks.com/news/the-acolyte-a-journey-to-the-filming-locations-part-1-madeira|text=The Acolyte: A journey to the filming locations Part 1: Madeira|archivedate=20241204220147}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Julian Foddy">{{Lucasfilm|url=news/julian-foddy-acolyte|text=''The Acolyte'' Visual Effects Supervisor Julian Foddy}}</ref> The character was credited only as "youngling" in the episode<ref name="LostFound" /> and she was first named in the [[2025]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

